### Today's GitHub Notes — AEM Assets

Topic: Metadata, Properties, Collections & Renditions

### 1\. Metadata in AEM Assets

Definition: Metadata is information that describes a digital asset, such as an image, video or PDF. It helps users search, identify and organize assets. Adobe Experience Manager

Example: For a campus food ordering website, a food image may have:

* Title: Chicken Burger

* Description: Burger with cheese

* Format: JPEG

* Tags: Food, Burger

* Copyright: Image usage rights

### 2\. Metadata vs Properties

| Metadata                             | Properties                                                             |
| ------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Information describing an asset      | The interface used to view or edit an asset's information and settings |
| Includes title, tags and description | Can display metadata and other asset details                           |
| Helps with searching and organizing  | Helps users inspect and modify available fields                        |

Remember: Metadata is the information; Properties is where you can view or edit much of that information in AEM Assets.

### 3\. Collections in AEM Assets

A collection groups related assets without creating duplicate copies of the original files. Assets can come from different folders. Adobe Experience Manager

Types of collections:

* Static collection: You manually add or remove assets.

* Smart collection: Assets are included automatically when they match defined search criteria.

Example: Create a `Food Menu Images` collection for your campus food ordering project.

### 4\. Renditions in AEM Assets

A rendition is a version of an original asset created for a particular purpose, such as a thumbnail or a web-optimized image. Adobe Experience Manager

